jobs.description:
The Senior Director of Operations is a senior management role within the company's operations management framework. Responsible for coordinating business operations, process management, resource allocation, operational performance, and cross-departmental execution, this role drives the effective implementation of the company's operational goals.

Typically responsible for the operations management of a large business division, multiple business units, or a major region, this position bridges senior management and operational teams. It translates corporate strategy and business objectives into concrete operational plans and enhances overall organizational operational efficiency and execution capabilities through process optimization, performance management, cost control, and team leadership.

Job Level
Senior Director (Senior Management)

Department
Operations

Reporting To
Chief Operating Officer (COO) / Vice President of Operations / General Manager / President

Location
USA (Specific office location determined by company needs)

Employment Type
Full-time

Key Responsibilities

I. Operational Strategy and Execution
- Formulate medium- to long-term operational strategies and annual operational plans for the department or business unit;
- Translate corporate strategy into operational goals, execution plans, and key actions;
- Adjust operational strategies in a timely manner based on business development and market changes;
- Oversee the execution progress of operational plans and key tasks;
- Ensure core operational goals are implemented according to plan.

II. Business Operations Management
- Assume full responsibility for the daily operations management of the assigned business division;
- Establish operational processes, management standards, and execution mechanisms;
- Oversee business activities, service delivery, and operational quality;
- Identify operational bottlenecks and drive their resolution;
- Enhance the overall operational stability and execution efficiency of the business unit.

III. Operational Performance Management
- Establish operational KPIs, OKRs, and performance management systems;
- Monitor key metrics such as revenue, costs, efficiency, quality, and service levels;
- Build operational dashboards and management reporting systems;
- Analyze the gap between actual business results and targets;
- Drive the formulation and execution of improvement plans for underperforming areas.

IV. Process Optimization and Operational Excellence
- Identify key process issues impacting efficiency, costs, and customer experience;
- Drive the standardization, optimization, and automation of core business processes;
- Establish mechanisms for continuous improvement and operational excellence;
- Promote the replication of best practices across teams and business units;
- Continuously enhance operational maturity and organizational execution capabilities.

V. Resource and Cost Management
- Manage planning for operations personnel, budgets, and business resources;
- Optimize resource allocation based on business priorities;
- Monitor operational costs, personnel efficiency, and resource utilization rates;
- Identify opportunities to reduce costs and boost productivity;
- Ensure alignment between operational resources and business needs.

VI. Cross-functional Collaboration
- Collaborate with sales, marketing, finance, product, technology, and customer-facing teams;
- Coordinate cross-departmental operational plans and key business projects;
- Resolve conflicts regarding resources, processes, and execution priorities;
- Drive business teams to collaborate toward unified operational goals;
- Establish efficient mechanisms for operational communication and issue escalation.

VII. Risk and Quality Management
- Establish mechanisms for identifying, assessing, monitoring, and escalating operational risks;
- Oversee operational, quality, and service risks within key business processes;
- Conduct root cause analysis and implement corrective actions for major operational issues;
- Ensure operational activities comply with corporate policies and applicable requirements;
- Establish emergency response mechanisms for major operational incidents.

VIII. Digitalization and Operational Analytics
- Drive the datafication, digitalization, and automation of operations;
- Collaborate with IT and data teams to optimize operational systems and tools;
- Leverage data analytics to support operational decision-making;
- Drive the use of AI, automation, and digital tools to enhance operational efficiency;
- Establish capabilities for real-time monitoring and analysis of operational data.

IX. Team and Organizational Development
- Lead senior operations management and execution teams;
- Build a talent pipeline comprising operations managers, directors, and specialists;
- Oversee recruitment, training, and development for key roles;
- Establish mechanisms for team performance management, incentives, and career development;
- Cultivate an operational culture characterized by high execution, data-driven decision-making, and continuous improvement. Requirements

Education
- Bachelor’s degree or higher in Business Administration, Operations Management, Economics, Engineering, Supply Chain Management, or a related field;
- MBA, EMBA, or relevant Master’s degree preferred.

Work Experience
- 20+ years of experience in operations management, business operations, or corporate management;
- 15+ years of experience in senior operations management;
- Experience as a Senior Director, Director, VP of Operations, or in a similar senior management role preferred;
- Experience managing large business units, multiple teams, or cross-regional operations;
- Experience in budget, resource, performance, and cost management;
- Experience in SaaS, Technology, Enterprise Services, FinTech, or Professional Services preferred.

Professional Competencies

- Ability to formulate and execute operational strategies;
- Familiarity with business operations and operational excellence;
- Proficiency in process optimization, continuous improvement, and operational standardization;
- Competence in budgeting, cost management, and resource allocation;
- Proficiency in operational performance and data analysis;
- Ability to coordinate cross-departmental projects and resolve complex issues;
- Competence in risk, quality, and business continuity management. Core Competencies

- Operations Management
- Business Operations
- Operational Excellence
- Process Improvement
- Performance Management
- Resource Planning
- Cost Management
- Business Analytics
- Risk Management
- Change Management
- Cross-functional Leadership
- Executive Communication

Preferred Background

Experience in one or more of the following areas is preferred:
Business Operations · Operations Management · Operational Excellence · Process Improvement · Continuous Improvement · Performance Management · Resource Planning · Cost Optimization · Business Transformation · Change Management · Service Operations · Program Management · Digital Transformation · SaaS · Enterprise Software · Technology · FinTech · Artificial Intelligence (AI) · Professional Services

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
- Operational goal achievement rate;
- Operational efficiency improvement rate;
- Operational cost reduction rate;
- Core business process cycle time;
- Resource utilization rate;
- Team productivity;
- Service quality compliance rate;
- SLA achievement rate;
- Budget adherence rate;
- Timeliness of operational issue resolution;
- Customer satisfaction;
- Key project completion rate;
- ROI of operational improvement projects;
- Key talent retention rate.

Show more

Show less

Seniority level

Director

Employment type

Full-time

Industries

Government Administration

